  "text": "Maqam Awj ‘Iraq A member of the Maqam Sikah Family Maqam Index Pronunciation of Awj ‘Iraq Click the notes and hold using the mouse to hear them play. Maqam Awj ‘Iraq is a version of Maqam Rahat al-Arwah/Maqam Huzam and Maqam ‘Iraq whose sayr starts at the octave tonic and descends to the tonic – though it shares most of the same ajnas as Maqam Huzam . The Maqam Awj ‘Iraq scale starts with the root Jins Sikah on the tonic , then Jins Hijaz on the 3 rd degree followed by another Jins Sikah on the 8 th degree. Explore other maqamat in the Maqam Sikah Family . Watch a 1-minute sample Violin Taqsim in Maqam Awj ‘Iraq by Sami Abu Shumays. Muwashah Ya Samiri Da‘a Sabri Muhammad Khayri Muwashah Hayya Wa Nadim Samer Nashar",
